{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3536","id":4763461080,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABG-yl2A","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3536","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3536.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3536.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3536","number":3536,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"policy/v2: skip via resolution when the policy has no via grants","user":{"login":"joscdk","id":2535140,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzUxNDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2535140?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk","html_url":"https://github.com/joscdk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joscdk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"What happened:\r\n- After upgrading to 0.29, we run about 450 nodes, and headscale saturated an 8 vCPU host every weekday.\r\n- A CPU profile put 82% of CPU in buildTailPeers → RoutesForPeer → ViaRoutesForPeer → AutoGroup.Resolve.\r\n- Our policy has no via grants at all.\r\n\r\nWhat the function does:\r\n- It is called once per peer in every map response.\r\n- It converts every ACL to grants, one grant per destination, and resolves every grant's sources and destinations against all nodes.\r\n- Only then does it check Via.\r\n- Without a via grant the result is always empty, so all of that work is discarded.\r\n\r\nCommit 1: the fix\r\n- Return early if no grant in pol.Grants has via.\r\n- The result is guaranteed unchanged: only via grants add to it, and ACLs can't carry via (aclToGrants never sets it).\r\n- Benchmarks:\r\n\r\n| Policy, 1,000 nodes | Before    | After                |\r\n|---------------------|-----------|----------------------|\r\n| ACL-only (global)   | 21.8 µs   | ~9 ns, 0 allocations |\r\n| self                | 45.0 µs   | ~9 ns, 0 allocations |\r\n| via                 | unchanged | unchanged            |\r\n\r\nCommit 2:\r\n- Resolve grants lazily when via is present. Non-via grants are only read once a via grant matched, and destinations only for grants that match the viewer.\r\n- via-mixed, 1,000 nodes: 69.0 µs → 11.6 µs.\r\n- Policy that is only a via grant: about 5% slower (8.1 → 8.6 µs).\r\n- Say you're happy to drop it if they'd rather keep this minimal.\r\n\r\nReal-fleet check:\r\n- Production export: 375 nodes, 245 users, real routes. All 62,850 peer pairs went from 84 s total on 0.29.4 to 0.55 ms.\r\n- Separately, rewriting our acls as grants was our interim workaround, about 3.3×. That matches what the #3512 reporter found.\r\n\r\nTests:\r\n- New subtest no_via_grant_returns_empty, plus BenchmarkViaRoutesForPeer.\r\n- Existing via tests pass. policy/..., state, mapper and -race pass.\r\n- Lint is clean.\r\n\r\nLast line: Fixes #3512","created_at":"2026-10-06T19:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-07T08:17:47Z","closed_at":"2026-10-06T19:11:00Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2ab5a87b7a7921a1a61a4bb72ff7197165270b1e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use